# P3-2 Task 6 (R7): -implicit_functors OWA fixture pair, "advisory arity"
# half. Byte-identical to implicit_functors_arity_plain.seam except for
# the directive line -- driven by TestImplicitFunctors in
# tests/test_implicit_functors.py. ``point/2`` IS declared here; under OWA
# its signature is advisory for keyword-free construction, so a reference at
# a DIFFERENT (here: greater) arity still compiles -- to a cell at the
# WRITTEN arity, not the declared one -- instead of the default over-arity
# compile error.
-implicit_functors
-module(implicit_functors_arity_owa, [point(x, y), p(A)])

p(point(10, 20, 30)),
